---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Recommendation Blocks — Case Study"
  description="Built product recommendations from zero to 80%+ adoption across five regions by designing trust-building three-tier ladder: Manual → Automated → Smart."
  article={{
    datePublished: "2025-09-03",
    dateModified: "2025-09-03",
  }}
>
  <article class="py-13">
    <nav class="mb-8">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="text-14 text-accent no-underline">← Back to case studies</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start mb-6">
      <h1 class="font-code text-32 font-semibold m-0 flex-1">Recommendation Blocks</h1>
      <button onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(window.location.href); this.textContent='Copied!'; setTimeout(() => this.textContent='Copy link', 2000);" class="px-4 py-2 border border-rule bg-transparent cursor-pointer font-code text-12 text-accent whitespace-nowrap rounded-[3px] transition-all duration-200" onmouseenter="this.style.borderColor='var(--accent)'" onmouseleave="this.style.borderColor='var(--rule)'">Copy link</button>
    </div>

    <p class="text-16 text-ink-2 mb-8 max-w-[65ch]">I built the company's product recommendation system from zero. Solved cold-start through three independent engines with CSM-driven tier selection: Curated (day 1, zero risk), Automated (pattern rules), Smart (live behavioral ranking). Multi-region serving under latency SLA.</p>

    <div class="flex gap-4 flex-wrap mb-8">
      <span class="metric-chip">day-1 deployment · no data required</span>
      <span class="metric-chip">5 regions · 200ms p99</span>
      <span class="metric-chip">built on the platform ↑</span>
    </div>

    <p class="font-code text-12 text-ink-3 mb-10">Node.js · Redis · MongoDB Atlas (multi-region) · ClickHouse · Google Pub/Sub</p>

    <!-- My Role -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-b border-rule pb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading mb-6">My Role</h2>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold text-accent mb-3">What I personally owned</h3>
        <div class="grid gap-3 max-w-[65ch]">
          <div><strong>Product architecture</strong> — designed three-tier trust model (Manual/Automated/Smart) to reduce merchant risk and enable gradual adoption</div>
          <div><strong>System design</strong> — architected multi-region serving, latency SLAs, and real-time ranking engine</div>
          <div><strong>Core implementation</strong> — architected and directed the Redis-backed live tier, MongoDB serving layer, and ranking algorithm; a small team (2–3 engineers) built and scaled it while I stayed close to product decisions and tradeoffs</div>
          <div><strong>Adoption strategy</strong> — worked with sales/success to position tiers, built tier progression measurement and ROI tracking</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold text-accent mb-3">What the product achieved</h3>
        <div class="grid gap-3 max-w-[65ch]">
          <div><strong>80%+ Smart-tier adoption</strong> — among merchants who trialled the tier</div>
          <div><strong>Multi-region latency</strong> — 200ms p99 across five regions with real-time ranking</div>
          <div><strong>Merchant trust</strong> — low-friction trust ladder moved from "risky feature" to default-on</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Context -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Context</h2>
      <p class="prose-body">The platform serves 200+ merchants across five regions. Merchants are SMBs with low transaction volume on day 1. Recommendation systems require behavioral data to produce quality results. Architecture challenge: ship day 1 with zero data, scale to algorithmic sophistication as data accumulates. Multi-region serving introduces latency constraints.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Problem -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Problem</h2>
      <p class="prose-body mb-6">New merchant on day 1: zero behavioral data. Live recommendation ranking needs statistical significance to produce quality results. Ship live ranking immediately and recommendations are garbage—merchants disable the feature. By day 30 when data exists, trust is already destroyed. Cannot recover.</p>

      <p class="prose-body mb-6">Architectural constraint: you need immediate value (day 1) with zero data, then scale to algorithmic sophistication as data accumulates. Cannot ship confident recommendations without data. Cannot gather data unless merchants use recommendations. Bootstrap problem.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 mt-6">
        <div class="p-5 bg-panel rounded">
          <div class="font-semibold text-accent mb-3">NAIVE APPROACH</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0">
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink mb-2">Ship live ranking day 1</li>
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink mb-2">Trains on zero data</li>
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink">Produces noise → merchants distrust system</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 bg-panel rounded">
          <div class="font-semibold text-accent mb-3">ARCHITECTURAL CHALLENGE</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0">
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink mb-2">Immediate value, zero data required</li>
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink mb-2">Bootstrap into sophisticated algorithms</li>
            <li class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-ink">Serve multi-region under 200ms latency</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Architecture</h2>
      <p class="prose-body mb-6">Three independent engines (Curated, Automated, Smart), tier selection driven by CSM discretion, not data availability. CSMs choose which tier per merchant based on trust and use case. Data flows live to Redis, then migrates to BigQuery after 30 minutes of session inactivity or session close. All logic and serving handled backend; client renders. Multi-region MongoDB for serving, ClickHouse for analytics.</p>

      <!-- Recommendation Architecture SVG -->
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 480" class="max-w-[65ch] w-full mb-6 block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <style>
            .rec-box { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--rule-2); stroke-width: 1.5; }
            .rec-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; fill: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
            .rec-label-small { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
            .rec-arrow { stroke: var(--ink-3); stroke-width: 2; fill: none; marker-end: url(#rec-arrowhead); }
          </style>
          <marker id="rec-arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
            <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="var(--ink-3)" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Tier progression (left column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">TIER PROGRESSION</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="40" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="65" text-anchor="middle">Manual</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="85" text-anchor="middle">CSM hand-picks</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="130"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="125" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="130" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="155" text-anchor="middle">Automated</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="175" text-anchor="middle">Rules · batch</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="190" x2="100" y2="220"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="215" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="220" width="160" height="80" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="250" text-anchor="middle">Smart</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="270" text-anchor="middle">(80%+ merchants)</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="285" text-anchor="middle">Live ranking · Redis</text>

        <!-- Multi-region serving (right column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="500" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">SERVING</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="40" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="70" text-anchor="middle">US · EU · APAC</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="100" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="130" text-anchor="middle">India · Brazil</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="160" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="185" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">200ms p99</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="205" text-anchor="middle">latency SLA</text>

        <!-- Latency tradeoff annotation -->
        <line style="stroke: var(--rule); stroke-width: 1;" x1="40" y1="340" x2="600" y2="340"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="360" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Latency-freshness tradeoff: read replicas lag 5–10s, acceptable for merchant UX</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="380" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Redis replication lag reduces on slow replica (fallback to cached tier), prioritizes speed over freshness</text>
      </svg>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Decisions -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Key decisions</h2>
      <ol class="max-w-[65ch] list-none p-0">
        <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-5">
          <strong>Tier selection driven by CSM judgment, not data triggers</strong><br/>
          <span class="text-ink-2">CSMs choose which tier per merchant—Curated for cautious starts, Automated for merchants with early transaction history, Smart for established stores ready for live behavioral ranking. No automatic progression based on transaction thresholds. Puts control in the hands of customer success, not an algorithm.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-5">
          <strong>Computation matched to data maturity</strong><br/>
          <span class="text-ink-2">Curated is static (no computation). Automated is batch rules (frequency > threshold). Smart is live ranking (statistical model). Cannot compute live ranking on day-7 data; would overfit.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-5">
          <strong>Redis-first serving, accept eventual consistency</strong><br/>
          <span class="text-ink-2">In-flight ranking state lost on Redis failure is acceptable for recommendations. Would not accept this for transactional orders. Latency requirement (200ms p99) demands in-memory serving.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink">
          <strong>Read replicas trade freshness for latency across regions</strong><br/>
          <span class="text-ink-2">Serving from regional replicas incurs 5-10s replication lag. Acceptable cost for 200ms p99 serving. Alternative: central Redis for all regions means 300-500ms network latency. Chose lower latency.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Execution -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Execution</h2>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">Data pipeline</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Behavioral events collected live into Redis. After 30 minutes of session inactivity or session close, data migrates to BigQuery for historical analysis. All logic and filtering happens backend; client is rendering only. Tier selection and ranking computed server-side, not pushed client-side.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">Multi-region serving under latency SLA</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Target: 200ms p99 across five regions (US, EU, APAC, India, Brazil). Deployed MongoDB instances in each region. Redis ranking cache replicated to regional instances with 5-10s lag. On replica lag, served cached tier (fallback to Automated) instead of blocking. Prioritized latency over freshness.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">Model validation before deploy</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Smart ranking trained on historical data. Before serving live, validated against held-out test sets. Checked for cardinality issues (one customer type over-indexed), signal stability (weights don't swing per retraining), and tail behavior (edge cases don't rank anomalously). Rejected models that failed validation.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">Monitoring & Rollback</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Tracked block click-through rate and block latency per tier. Anomalies (CTR drop >10%, latency spike) paged on-call. Could disable tiers independently if quality degraded. Built canary deployment for Smart tier: new model runs on 5% of traffic first, compared metrics to incumbent.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Impact -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Impact</h2>

      <div class="text-center mb-8 py-8 border-t border-b border-rule">
        <div class="text-56 font-semibold text-accent mb-3">200ms P99 · DAY 1</div>
        <div class="text-16 text-ink-2 max-w-[65ch] mx-auto">Deployed Curated recommendations on day 1 across five regions under latency SLA</div>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold text-accent mb-3">Technical achievement</h3>
        <ul class="max-w-[65ch] list-none p-0">
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-3">Cold-start solved by CSM-driven tier selection + three independent engines. CSMs choose tier (Curated, Automated, Smart) per merchant based on confidence and use case, not algorithm-triggered progression.</li>
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-3">Data pipeline: live to Redis, migrate to BigQuery after 30min inactivity or session close. All backend logic; client renders only. No client-side filtering or ranking logic.</li>
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-3">Multi-region serving with regional Redis + fallback caching. 200ms p99 latency across five regions despite 5-10s replication lag.</li>
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink">Model validation gate ensured Smart tier only served high-confidence rankings. Prevented garbage output from ruining system trust.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold text-accent mb-3">Scale</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Day-1 deployment (Curated tier, zero risk) · five regions · 200ms p99 latency · CSM-driven tier progression from Curated → Automated → Smart as merchants gain confidence</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I'd Change Today -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-heading">What I'd Change Today</h2>

      <div class="mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">What I'd Preserve</h3>
        <p class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink max-w-[65ch]">Three-tier architecture with CSM control. Giving customer success ownership over tier selection (not automation) meant we could start with Curated (zero risk), and CSMs could upgrade merchants to Automated/Smart as they gained confidence. Prevented shipping garbage output and losing trust on day 1.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-14 font-semibold mb-3">What I'd Change</h3>
        <ul class="max-w-[65ch] list-none p-0">
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-3"><strong>Canary deployments from day one.</strong> Built it later, but early validation would have caught model quality issues faster.</li>
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink mb-3"><strong>Feature flag for Smart tier per merchant.</strong> All-or-nothing rollout was risky. Gradual merchant cohort rollout would allow faster issue detection.</li>
          <li class="text-16 leading-[1.8] text-ink">​<strong>Separate model retraining from serving.</strong> Current design retrains synchronously, risks latency spikes. Async retraining into separate cache layer would decouple.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="py-13 border-t border-rule mt-13">
      <p class="font-code text-12 text-accent font-semibold mb-4">Next steps</p>
      <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0">
        <li class="mb-3">→ <a href="/case-studies/hard-problems" class="plain-link">See production incidents that shaped this design</a></li>
        <li class="mb-3">→ <a href="/resume" class="plain-link">Download my resume</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-next { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-top: 32px; margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
